<title>NORWAY: Transocean wins $50 mln Aasgard contract.</title>
<headline>Transocean wins $50 mln Aasgard contract.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian drilling and offshore service company Transocean ASA said on Tuesday it had won contracts worth $50 million for the Aasgard oil development in the Norwegian Sea.</p>
<p>The company said the deal would utilise the Transocean Searcher and Transocean Saga rigs.</p>
<p>Aasgard is operated by Norwegian state oil company Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil ).</p>
<p>-- Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
